<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nuapada district</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nuapada is a district in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh">Chhattisgarh</a>, with its headquarters at the town of Nuapada. It was created in 1993 from part of Kalahandi district. Largely rural and forested, it includes Khariar, the former seat of the Khariar princely estate, and the Sunabeda wildlife sanctuary.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nuapada-district.jpg" alt="Nuapada district" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sudhansu bhusan mishra · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yogeswar_Temple,_Patora.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
